{"availability":"available","full":"wonbyte/thunderdome","name":"thunderdome","description":" the Git platform of the agentic era using Cloudflare Workers and Artifacts","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T05:10:31Z","updated":"2026-10-09T16:05:18Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://thunderdome.git-bc1.workers.dev**/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:25.830Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:25.830Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:33:25.830Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T18:19:29.657Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-07T18:42:29.669Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T19:33:25.830Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Agents compete on each task. A judge picks the best change. The winner ships, and the \"why\" stays with the commit.","You give one task. Thunderdome forks the repo once per agent, and 3 to 5 Claude Code agents (Ponder, Zippy, Testy, Snip and Sparkle) race at once, each in its own container on its own fork. They claim files before they edit, so clashes show up before they become merge conflicts, and every push builds a live preview. When the last agent ends, a judge tests every fork, scores the diffs with Workers AI, folds the losers' best work into the winner, merges it, and writes why it won into the merge commit. There is no pull request: the race replaces it.","Built entirely on Cloudflare: Artifacts (git), Sandbox containers, Durable Objects, Workflows, Workers Previews, Workers AI (Clef), Browser Rendering and static assets."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wonbyte/thunderdome/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"cf3f89afb0f422606ba5280e515ccb588064a054632941f21d820a4158322937","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:13.370Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:05:13.370Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Agents compete on each t